Labcontainers interoperates with Containerlab, which is licensed under the
BSD 3-Clause License. The Go topology adapter imports Containerlab's native
configuration types. Python topology bindings are generated from its JSON
Schema, vendored in schemas/containerlab. The upstream license is included
there and in Python distributions as labcontainers/CONTAINERLAB-LICENSE.
Deployment uses the separately installed Containerlab executable.

Cloud-init network bindings are generated from Canonical cloud-init's network
v2 JSON Schema, vendored in schemas/cloud-init. The original license notice
(GPLv3 or Apache-2.0) is included there and in Python distributions as
labcontainers/CLOUD-INIT-LICENSE. These are configuration objects; cloud-init
itself remains the guest operating system's separately installed component.
